  "findings": [
    {
      "level": "warn",
      "id": "version-drift",
      "lines": [
        "Version drift: appinfo/info.xml says 0.1.10, package.json says 0.1.7.",
        "  The App Store and the server read info.xml; everything on the node side reads package.json. Whichever is behind, a release ends up carrying two version numbers, and only one of them reaches the user."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "warn",
      "id": "link-dead",
      "lines": [
        "7 links of appinfo/info.xml lead nowhere:",
        "  <website> https://codeberg.org/Conduction/nextcloud-petstore: HTTP 404",
        "  <bugs> https://codeberg.org/Conduction/nextcloud-petstore/issues: HTTP 404",
        "  <repository> https://codeberg.org/Conduction/nextcloud-petstore: HTTP 404",
        "  <documentation><user> https://codeberg.org/Conduction/nextcloud-petstore: HTTP 404",
        "  <documentation><admin> https://codeberg.org/Conduction/nextcloud-petstore: HTTP 404",
        "  <documentation><developer> https://codeberg.org/Conduction/nextcloud-petstore: HTTP 404",
        "  <screenshot> https://codeberg.org/Conduction/nextcloud-petstore/raw/branch/main/img/app-store.svg: HTTP 404",
        "  The App Store page shows these links as they are; a reader who follows one ends on an error page."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "warn",
      "id": "node-eol",
      "lines": [
        "engines.node ^20.0.0 in package.json admits only end-of-life Node lines: the release is built on Node 20, which reached end of life on 2026-04-30.",
        "  That Node receives no security fixes, and the lockfile is resolved for it. The oldest line still maintained is Node 22.",
        "  Node release dates from schedule.json in nodejs/Release, as of 2026-11-01."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "nextcloud-support",
      "lines": [
        "Declares Nextcloud 28 to 34; the oldest maintained major is 32 (as of 2026-09), the newest released 35 (the release tags of nextcloud/server).",
        "  min-version 28 reaches below the oldest maintained major (32), which means the code has to keep working with APIs that are no longer tested upstream."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "node-version",
      "lines": [
        "Node 20 stated in spec-validation.yml, within package.json engines.node ^20.0.0.",
        "  Not stated in .nvmrc, so nothing keeps the other places from drifting away from it."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "tooling",
      "lines": [
        "Tooling in the checkout: ESLint (eslint.config.js), Stylelint (stylelint.config.js), Psalm (psalm.xml), PHPUnit (phpunit.xml), REUSE (REUSE.toml).",
        " No PHP-CS-Fixer configuration: no coding standard is applied to the PHP sources, so formatting is settled in review instead of by a command.",
        " No EditorConfig configuration: indentation is whatever each contributor's editor does."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "unreferenced-dependencies",
      "lines": [
        "7 declared packages are named nowhere in the checkout: @babel/preset-env, vue-apexcharts, @cyclonedx/cyclonedx-npm, @typescript-eslint/eslint-plugin, @typescript-eslint/parser, eslint-import-resolver-alias, vue-eslint-parser.",
        "  Searched as literal names over 251 files, package.json excluded apart from its non-dependency fields, lockfiles excluded; then as an ESLint shorthand, as what TypeScript takes from a tsconfig, and as a peer of an installed package in package-lock.json. A package loaded some other way is not named anywhere either, so this is a list to check, not a list to remove."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "license-drift",
      "lines": [
        "Licence EUPL-1.2 (appinfo/info.xml, package.json, composer.json).",
        "  No LICENSES/ directory, so the licence text itself is not in the checkout, which is what REUSE and the distributions check for."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "ok",
      "id": "repository-link",
      "lines": [
        "appinfo/info.xml links its repository and its bug tracker."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "ok",
      "id": "php-support",
      "lines": [
        "PHP 8.3 is the floor in appinfo/info.xml and in composer.json, platform 8.3."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "ok",
      "id": "lockfiles",
      "lines": [
        "package-lock.json (lockfileVersion 3) and composer.lock in the checkout."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "ok",
      "id": "ncmake-bootstrap",
      "lines": [
        "The ncmake bootstrap stub is in place (21 lines).",
        "  make reads GNUmakefile and never Makefile; it runs only with make -f <name>."
      ]
    },
    {
